# 27. 🛠️ COMMON BEGINNER MISTAKES

## Mistake 1: Image not showing

Check:

<img src="myphoto.jpg">

Then check that the image actually exists in the correct folder.

---

## Mistake 2: Wrong filename

HTML:

<img src="myphoto.jpg">

Actual file:

MyPhoto.JPG

These may not match.

Always check:

- Filename
- Extension
- Folder
- Spelling

---

## Mistake 3: Forgetting to save

Use:

Ctrl + S

Then refresh the browser:

F5

---

## Mistake 4: Missing < or >

Correct:

<h1>Hello</h1>

Incorrect:

h1>Hello/h1>

Remember:

<  → Opening symbol
>  → Closing symbol
/  → Closing tag

---

## Mistake 5: Using too many <br>

Avoid:

<br><br><br><br><br>

for spacing.

Use CSS for proper spacing.

---

# 28. 💡 HTML TIPS & TRICKS

### Tip 1: Understand instead of memorizing

Do not try to memorize every HTML tag.

Ask:

1. What does this tag do?
2. Why am I using it?
3. Where should I use it?

---

### Tip 2: Change the code yourself

Instead of only writing:

<h1>My Name is Nikitha</h1>

try:

<h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>

Then:

<h1>My Portfolio</h1>

This helps build understanding.

---

### Tip 3: Use indentation

Good:

<body>

    <h1>Hello</h1>

    <p>Hello World</p>

</body>

Avoid writing everything on one line.

---

### Tip 4: Understand parent and child elements

Example:

<ul>
    <li>Java</li>
    <li>SQL</li>
</ul>

Think:

ul
├── li
└── li

This becomes very useful when learning CSS and JavaScript.

---

### Tip 5: File paths are extremely important

Many beginner web-development problems come from:

- Wrong filename
- Wrong folder
- Wrong path
- Wrong extension

Always check these first when something does not work.

