# 29. 🎤 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS

## Q1. What is HTML?

HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It is used to create the structure and content of webpages.

## Q2. Is HTML a programming language?

No. HTML is a markup language, not a programming language.

## Q3. What is <!DOCTYPE html>?

It tells the browser that the document uses HTML5.

## Q4. Difference between <head> and <body>?

<head> contains information about the webpage, while <body> contains the content displayed to the user.

## Q5. Difference between <h1> and <p>?

<h1> is used for a main heading, while <p> is used for a paragraph.

## Q6. What is href?

href specifies the destination of a hyperlink.

## Q7. What is src?

src specifies the source/location of an external resource such as an image.

## Q8. What is alt?

alt provides alternative text for an image. It is useful when an image cannot be displayed and also helps accessibility.

## Q9. Difference between <ul> and <ol>?

<ul> creates an unordered/bullet list.

<ol> creates an ordered/numbered list.

## Q10. What does target="_blank" do?

It opens the link in a new browser tab/window.

